  "articleBody": "Designing a tiny home specifically for guests is a bit different from designing your primary residence. It’s all about creating a welcoming, self-sufficient space that makes visitors feel right at home, even in a compact footprint. Zen Tiny Homes knows how to maximize every square inch, turning small spaces into intentional, comfortable, and high-functioning guest retreats.\n\nFirst up, privacy is key. Guests appreciate their own entrance and a layout that offers a sense of separation from the main house. Think about soundproofing and thoughtful window placement. Next, focus on essential amenities. A full bathroom and a functional kitchenette are usually must-haves. Even in a small space, a place to prepare simple meals and a comfortable shower make a huge difference. Storage is another big one; your guests won't be bringing their whole lives, but a closet or some clever built-ins for their belongings will be much appreciated. Consider flexible living areas – a sofa that converts to a bed, a dining table that folds away – so the space can adapt to different needs. Lastly, make it inviting! Warm lighting, durable finishes, and a touch of local charm can really elevate the guest experience. Remember, we design these homes around how people *actually* live and use the space, ensuring functionality without sacrificing style.\n\nIf you're dreaming of a perfect guest hideaway, reach out to Zen Tiny Homes. We can help you design a space that’s both practical and beautiful, truly making the most out of less.",
